# L §5.16 Samples: u = (k + 1/2)/2^64 with k the first 8 bytes of SHA-256("address|S|p") read big-endian (the
# uniforms below are that stated rule computed for these addresses; scratch/refcore-r2/gen/hashes.py):
#   draw|1|1 00a1d43157219469 u < 1/2;  draw|1|2 8ec4354902549e2a u > 1/2;  draw|1|3 ebce717fe397e00d u > 1/2;
#   draw|1|4 3a6978c343f06fe4 u < 1/2;  emp|1|1..4: u < 1/2, < 1/2, > 1/2, < 1/2;  emp|3|1 > 1/2, emp|3|2 < 1/2.
# discrete(1, 1 over [ka, kb]) has quantile(D, u) = ka for u <= 1/2, else kb (type 1, index order); empirical(0, 2)
# gives 0 for u <= 1/2, else 2 ("one of the values").
# share(draw == ka) over seed 1: paths 1 and 4, "2 of 4" and 0.5, standard error sqrt(0.5 × 0.5 / 4) = 0.25.
# mean(emp) over seed 3: samples 2 and 0, mean 1, s^2 = (1 + 1)/(2 - 1) = 2, standard error sqrt(2/2) = 1.
# quantile(emp, 50 %) over seed 3: the smallest value with at least 1 of 2 samples at or below it: 0, now with its
# Maritz-Jarrett standard error (round 19, GD-3; refcore's figure, its weights given both ways in
# L5_16_quantile_se_check).  mean(emp where draw == ka) over seed 1 keeps paths 1 and 4 (emp 0 and 0): mean 0, standard error 0,
# "2 of 4 paths".  The horizon is the law date the facts are read at (at reader: the ask's law).
# (Writer 8: empirical is gone (L §2.3); emp is now discrete(eq[k] for k in ks), eq = 1 at both keys, and its
# value is read as ev = vals[emp], the form L §5.16 gives for "one of n known values drawn with equal weight",
# e[discrete(1 for k in IDX)]: the same uniforms, and the samples 0 and 2 as before, emp itself now ka or kb.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index ks = [ka, kb]
input w[k in ks]: num
input vals[k in ks]: num
input eq[k in ks]: num
input q25: num
input neg: num
input y1: num
def draw: dist = discrete(w[k] for k in ks) at reader
def emp: dist = discrete(eq[k] for k in ks) at reader
def ev: num = vals[emp] at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  w[ka] = 1
  w[kb] = 1
  vals[ka] = 0
  vals[kb] = 2
  eq[*] = 1
  q25 = 0.25
  neg = -1
  y1 = 1

ask s1: share(draw == ka) law 2026-06-30 paths 4 seed 1
ask s2: mean(ev) law 2026-06-30 paths 2 seed 3
ask s3: quantile(ev, 50 %) law 2026-06-30 paths 2 seed 3
ask s4: mean(ev where draw == ka) law 2026-06-30 paths 4 seed 1
=== expect
s1: 2 of 4, 0.5 (standard error 0.25; 4 paths; horizon 2026-06-30)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
s2: 1 (standard error 1; 2 paths; horizon 2026-06-30)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
s3: 0 (standard error 0.866025; 2 paths; horizon 2026-06-30)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
s4: 0 (standard error 0; 2 of 4 paths; horizon 2026-06-30)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
